// Change: new rule
// Title: YOOtheme Pro Webshell Suspicious Command Execution
// Sigma ID: 2d1f3c03-ef50-439e-800b-3d5f5525a21a
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Saksham Bhattarai
// Date: 2026-10-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, persistence, T1059.003, T1505.003
// Description: Detects command execution patterns associated with webshell activity reported during
//   exploitation of CVE-2026-102785, including command interpreter execution of reconnaissance
//   commands and scanner markers.
// False positives:
//   - Web applications legitimately invoking command interpreters
// References:
//   - https://github.com/PaloAltoNetworks/Unit42-timely-threat-intel/blob/47b53a06affd56b4fefbbcb1fb9fdaf88e3cca5e/2026-10-26-exploitation-of-CVE-2026-102785.txt
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/1c002158db1d36aaf9366d1c551476a7264585ec/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_webshell_command_execution_yootheme.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\httpd.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\httpd-ssl.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\php-cgi.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\w3wp.exe") and FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "echo YTS" or ProcessCommandLine contains "uname -a" or ProcessCommandLine contains "whoami" or ProcessCommandLine contains "crossdomain.xml")
